l},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","number":22,"title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-08-25T21:14:48Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T18:44:41Z","closed_at":"2025-08-27T00:02:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109970","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109970","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109970.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109970.patch","merged_at":"2025-08-27T00:02:33Z"},"body":"Fixes #109531\r\n\r\nThis PR should bring debanding back to a state where it is equivalent or better than the Godot 4.4.1 behaviour in all cases. To do this, SMAA now has debanding support built-in, which allows debanding to correctly be applied directly before quantization to integer values.\r\n\r\nThis approach means the debanding dithering is applied twice to a very similar 10 bit buffer when using the Mobile rendering method with HDR 2D enabled and SMAA enabled. This makes the dithering noise more visible than necessary, but it doesn't worthwhile to add in even more logic for this very specific scenario. This is not an issue when the scene buffer and swapchain buffer have different formats, like in Forward+ or Mobile with HDR 2D disabled: in these cases, if two debanding passes happen, the first debanding will be applied to 10 bit linear and the second debanding will be applied to 8 bit nonlinear, which is the ideal behaviour.\r\n\r\nFor spatial upscaling (FSR 1.0 and MetalFX (Spatial)), behaviour similar to Godot 4.4.1 has been reintroduced: the debanding pattern will be applied prematurely and spatial upscaling will be applied afterwards. This creates suboptimal results, as noted in the comments of this PR, but for the sake of maintaining the \"better than nothing\" approach of Godot 4.4.1, I think this is a reasonable compromise for now.\r\n\r\nIn the future we can look at introducing a full new pass that applies debanding after spatial scaling.\r\n\r\nFinally, I have changed the \"reserved\" push constant names to \"pad\" in SMAA, since these appear to be padding and are not actually meant to be reserved for anything in particular.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109970/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109970/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}